- op: discuss  # 3adf
  at: '2026-07-01T23:23:37Z'  # 3adf
  by: agent  # 3adf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3adf
  clock: 4  # 3adf
  nonce: 3adf  # 3adf
  message: "DONE via ADR-0038 rulings 2+4 (dev 880cb6775a + prior INV-kudug #74). Both facets the item + its discussion flagged are resolved: (facet a / constructors) the access_mode applicability gate makes instantiates Declared-N/A, so the dataflow classifier no longer stamps ANY instantiates edge -> access_mode=None (was 5992 self-corpus stamps). This resolves BOTH sub-facets from the P1 discussion at once: facet-2 'instantiation is not an access, access_mode meaningless on instantiates' (no stamp at all now) and facet-1 'per-call-site nondeterministic assignment for the same construct' (mooted — there is no access_mode on instantiates to be nondeterministic). (facet b / in-memory collection mutations) python.yaml maps .append/.extend/.add -> 'mutate' not 'write' (ruling 4) -> behavioral: items.append(1)/items.extend([2]) now carry access_mode='mutate', so a dataflow-write-position mutation is no longer conflated with an I/O 'write'. Live repro: a 3-line list-mutation file yields mutate; an instantiation yields None. awaits_bakeoff_validation (blast-radius emission change)."  # 3adf
